      "message": "These names have more meaning regarding the I2C bus, as opposed to the USB-C port number.\n\nI also think we might need another level in the devicetree.  Maybe something like:\n\nusbc {\n    port0: usb-port0 {\n        compatible \"usbc-port\";\n        bc12 {\n            compatible \u003d \"pericom,pi3usb9201\";\n        };\n        tcpc {\n            compatible \u003d \"parade,ps8805\";\n        };\n        ppc {\n            compatible \u003d \"silergy,syv682x\";\n        };\n    };\n    port1: usb-port1 { ... }\n    port2: usb-port2 { ... }\n};\n\nEach driver would then use DT_FOREACH_STATUS_OKAY(compat, fn) to iterate over all USB ports, finding the enabled drivers.\n\nThe usb_port probably needs it\u0027s own driver, so we can do the equivalent of DT_INST_BUS() to associate the USB port number with each BC12, TCPC, PPC, driver initialized.\n\nI\u0027m not sure how feasible this is before the full USB-C upstream work.",
